 ## Overview
-Pointcloud to Sparse Voxel Grid Conversion maps a set of 3D points into a sparse grid of voxel centers and associated features, retaining only occupied cells. It differs from dense voxelization by using hash maps or sparse arrays to store only occupied cells, and from simple occupancy voxelization by optionally storing averaged geometric and color data per voxel [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. This method serves as the core voxelization step in pipelines converting point clouds to sparse voxel representations for downstream rendering or USD export [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
+Pointcloud to Sparse Voxel Grid Conversion maps a set of 3D points into a sparse grid of voxel centers and associated features, retaining only occupied cells [S1, unofficial]. It converts a point cloud into a sparse voxel grid representation, storing only voxels that contain points [S2, unofficial]. This method serves as the core voxelization step in pipelines converting point clouds to sparse voxel representations for downstream rendering or USD export [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
 
